Etienne Crozetière
	
gfortran projet1.f90 selec_get.c -o projet1
./projet1


The project consists of creating a Brick Breaker game developed in Fortran. The player controls a paddle that moves horizontally to bounce a ball and destroy the bricks located at the top of the screen.

User Guide : 

When launching the program, a first prompt asks the user to enter the number of rows for the grid, then a second prompt asks them to specify the number of columns. 
To control the paddle, the commands are as follows: 
Move left : key g
Move right  : key h

The 'X' bricks are standard bricks, while the '2' bricks are special bricks. 
